&lt;h2 id="source-code-analysis"&gt;Source code analysis&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The code is simple. Basically, it allows us to enter a prime number $p$ and a number $n$ such that $13 &amp;lt; n &amp;lt; p$ to create a &lt;a target="_blank" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shamir%27s_Secret_Sharing"&gt;Shamir Secret Sharing scheme&lt;/a&gt;. The polynomial $P(x)$ of degree $n - 1$ will have random coefficients in $\mathbb{F}_p$ and the secret $S$ will be the independent term ($S = P(0)$). We are given these shares: $\big\{P(1), \dots, P(n - 1)\big\}$.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>